  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EUROFRONT - Support to the Fight against Human Trafficking and Migrant Smuggling in Latin America</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the project is to support the fight against human trafficking and smuggling of migrants at national and regional levels in Latin America with focus in the South America sub-region. This project is part of a two-fold action being led by the European Commission, that aims to contribute to security, improved respect for, and protection of, human rights and social and economic development at national and regional levels in Latin America, from an Integrated Border Management perspective. It will focus on four significant land borders in South America, including Rumichaca, Desaguadero, Bermejo-Aguas Blancas and the Tripler Border; covering Argentina, Brazil, Bolivia, Colombia, Ecuador, Paraguay and Peru, with impact in other countries in South America, Central America and the Caribbean.</narrative>
  </description>
